    "legend": "Small tissue fragment of atypical cells with elongated nuclei, showing a very high N:C&nbsp;ratio and nuclear moulding, and atypical single cells with irregular nuclei, finely granular chromatin, and no prominent nucleoli in the background. Normal ciliated bronchial cells are present at 5&nbsp;o&rsquo;clock centrally, for size comparison (bronchial brushing, Giemsa).",
