    "title": "<p>Differential diagnosis of neuroendocrine carcinomas</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Claire W. Michael",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 697.4pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Characteristic features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Immunocytochemistry</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Singly scattered bronchial cells</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nucleus slightly smaller, with fine chromatin</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Columnar ciliated cells</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Adjacent goblet cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative for NE markers</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Small cell carcinoma and large cell carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">More atypia and necrosis, plentiful mitoses and nuclear moulding</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Plexiform capillaries absent in SCNEC</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">More cohesive tissue fragments</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Ki-67 &gt;&nbsp;40%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Merkel cell carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Small cohesive tissue fragments or single cells</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Scant cytoplasm, moulding, and crush artefact</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Atypia at least focally</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for NE markers</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive CK20 (dot-like)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for MCPyV large T antigen</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Adenocarcinoma of lung</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">3D tissue fragments, coarse chromatin, prominent nuclei</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">SAPC absent</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Vacuolated cytoplasm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">TTF1 is not helpful</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Negative for NE markers and positive for napsin&nbsp;A and CK7</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Adenoid cystic carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Tight small blue cell tissue fragments</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Scant cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Metachromatic material +/&minus;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Demonstrates dual luminal epithelial and subluminal myoepithelial cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative for NE markers and TTF1</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Luminal epithelium positive for low-molecular-weight keratin and KIT</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Abluminal myoepithelial cells positive for p63/p40, SMA, S100, and SOX10</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">MYB positive in most cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Lobular carcinoma of breast</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Plasmacytoid cells with high N:C&nbsp;ratio</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Variable nuclear atypia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">SAPC absent</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Intracytoplasmic lumina</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Negative for NE markers</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Positive for GATA3, ER, and PR</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Variable reaction with GCDFP and mammaglobin</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Small discohesive cells</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Scant cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">SAPC absent</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Numerous fragments of lymphoid cell cytoplasm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for lymphoid markers</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative for keratins and NE markers</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Oncocytic neoplasms</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Sheets, tissue fragments, or single cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Large cells with abundant granular cytoplasm</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Prominent nuclei</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Negative for NE markers</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Additional stains depending on primary origin</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Melanoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Plasmacytoid, round to oval to spindle cells</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Moderate dusty cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Large nuclei with prominent cherry-red nucleoli</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Background melanin pigment +/&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative for NE markers and keratins</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for S100, HMB45, melan-A (MART1), and SOX10</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Paraganglioma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.05pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Small tissue fragments or single cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Fine chromatin</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Moderate to abundant pale cytoplasm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Positive for NE markers</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Negative for cytokeratins</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">S100 highlights sustentacular cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">NE, neuroendocrine; MCPyV, Merkel cell polyomavirus; SAPC, salt-and-pepper chromatin; SCNEC, small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma; TTF1, thyroid transcription factor&nbsp;1.</p>",
